From: Lars Slettan Øydneskleiv <larsoyd@github.com>
Date: Mon, 24 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] wmvcore: Implement IWMProfileManager::LoadProfileByData.

IWMProfileManager::LoadProfileByData is a fully-specified Windows Media
Format SDK API: given the profile-XML text format used throughout WMSDK
(the same schema Windows Movie Maker embeds as PE resources for its own
default capture/preview profiles, and the same schema its on-disk
exported .prx profile files use), it parses it and returns a working
IWMProfile object exposing the parsed streams' types, bitrates, buffer
windows, names and full WM_MEDIA_TYPE (WAVEFORMATEX / VIDEOINFOHEADER +
BITMAPINFOHEADER) media types.

Wine's implementation was a complete stub - FIXME(...); return
E_NOTIMPL; - never touching its IWMProfile** out-parameter. This is
directly observable as a real-world compatibility bug, not just a
missing conformance detail: Windows Movie Maker 6.0's own
CWMTProfileManager::CreateProfileFromData wrapper detects the E_NOTIMPL
failure but (a defensive-code bug of its own, never exercised against
genuine Windows, where this call does not fail for the application's
own bundled, known-good profiles) returns S_FALSE instead of
propagating a real failure code, leaving its own out-parameter NULL.
Its caller three frames up, CWMTProfileManager::LoadApplicationProfiles,
never NULL-checks the resulting pointer before dereferencing it, and
crashes - during the application's post-startup idle-loop
initialization, a few seconds after its main window has already
rendered successfully.

This implements profile-XML parsing end to end in a new
dlls/wmvcore/profile.c:

 - wm_profile_create_from_xml() wraps the caller's in-memory profile
   text in an IStream (via CreateStreamOnHGlobal, the same pattern
   dlls/taskschd/task.c already uses for its own in-memory task-XML
   strings) and drives it through xmllite's real, already-tested
   IXmlReader (dlls/xmllite) with a small explicit element-context
   stack - the schema (<profile>, <streamconfig>, <wmmediatype>,
   <waveformatex>, <videomediaprops>, <videoinfoheader>, <rcsource>,
   <rctarget>, <bitmapinfoheader>, <dataunitextension>,
   <streamprioritization>, <stream>) is a small closed set of flat
   attribute bags nested at most four levels deep, confirmed by
   extracting and inspecting all 31 RT_PRX profile resources a real
   Windows Movie Maker 6.0 install embeds, so no general-purpose
   tree/DOM handling is needed.
 - GUID-valued attributes (majortype/subtype) are parsed via
   CLSIDFromString, already available through combase, rather than a
   hand-rolled GUID parser or a hardcoded subtype table.
 - A new struct wm_profile (IWMProfile3) and struct wm_profile_stream
   (IWMStreamConfig + IWMMediaProps, the same interface-splitting COM
   idiom dlls/winegstreamer/wm_reader.c's struct stream_config already
   uses) implement the profile/stream object graph. Unlike wm_reader.c's
   read-only reflection of an already-open GStreamer-demuxed stream,
   these are self-contained, freely settable objects built straight
   from the parsed attributes - real GetStreamCount/GetStream/
   GetStreamByNumber, and real IWMStreamConfig/IWMMediaProps get/set
   pairs for stream type, number, name, connection name, bitrate,
   buffer window and full media type. Methods with no bearing on this
   codepath (CreateNewStream/AddStream/RemoveStream/mutual-exclusion/
   stream-prioritization/storage-format/profile-ID) are left as the same
   FIXME()+E_NOTIMPL stub pattern already used throughout this DLL.

Confirmed against a real-fault harness (harness/wmprofile-loadbydata/ in
the Movie Maker Wine investigation tree) that drives the exact same
LoadProfileByData call path with a small, self-authored profile-XML
string covering the full schema above (one audio stream, one video
stream, a dataunitextension and a streamprioritization block, and an
entity-escaped description to exercise xmllite's entity decoding):
fails with E_NOTIMPL against the unpatched stub, passes - correct
stream count, stream types, bitrates, buffer windows, and correctly
round-tripped WAVEFORMATEX/VIDEOINFOHEADER/BITMAPINFOHEADER field
values and entity-decoded description - with this patch applied. Also
confirmed against the real Windows Movie Maker 6.0 application: with
this patch, the main window survives well past the point
CWMTProfileManager::LoadApplicationProfiles previously crashed
(moviemk+0x404722, a NULL-pointer dereference a few seconds into the
app's post-startup idle-loop initialization), and a full err/fixme
trace of the process shows zero wmvcore fixme lines and zero
unhandled-exception markers across all 31 of the application's bundled
default profiles.
---
diff --git a/dlls/wmvcore/Makefile.in b/dlls/wmvcore/Makefile.in
index bf9d47c986b..72eb7e92c1c 100644
--- a/dlls/wmvcore/Makefile.in
+++ b/dlls/wmvcore/Makefile.in
@@ -1,6 +1,6 @@
 MODULE    = wmvcore.dll
 IMPORTLIB = wmvcore
-IMPORTS   = kernel32 combase
+IMPORTS   = kernel32 combase xmllite
 DELAYIMPORTS = winegstreamer
 
 VER_FILEDESCRIPTION_STR = "Wine Media Playback dll"
@@ -8,5 +8,6 @@ VER_PRODUCTVERSION      = 12,0,7601,17514
 
 SOURCES = \
 	async_reader.c \
+	profile.c \
 	wmvcore_main.c \
 	writer.c
diff --git a/dlls/wmvcore/profile.c b/dlls/wmvcore/profile.c
new file mode 100644
index 00000000000..87a2f24633a
--- /dev/null
+++ b/dlls/wmvcore/profile.c
@@ -0,0 +1,1390 @@
+/*
+ * Copyright 2026 Lars Slettan Øydneskleiv <larsoyd@github.com>
+ *
